Google's internal USB-camera table omits the MSI webcam (30c9:0042), so the
USB HAL advertises it as external. Apps selecting only front/back cameras
may therefore report no camera. Mark this exact USB ID front-facing without
inventing lens/sensor calibration or changing other cameras and effects.
Drop when Google's table includes this webcam or discovery classifies it
correctly without the override. Physical preview/capture must be retested.

--- a/etc/camera/internal_usb_camera_info.txtpb
+++ b/etc/camera/internal_usb_camera_info.txtpb
@@ -1,6 +1,12 @@
 use_hardware_jpeg_decoder: true
 face_detection_input_width: 320
 camera_modules {
+  key: "30c9:0042" # MSI Modern 15 B7M integrated webcam
+  value {
+    facing: FACING_FRONT
+  }
+}
+camera_modules {
   key: "0408:4052" # Quanta YHVA-5
   value {
     lens_info {
